Hanako (@hanakoxbt) — "Loops and Graphs"
  https://x.com/hanakoxbt/status/2091515787366306154
  License: none declared (a public post; no code accompanies it).
  No text copied — the ten claims were audited against this kit's code by a
  subagent first, and only the five that had no existing mechanism were
  implemented, in the kit's own words and structure. Inspired: the false-edge
  validator rule, i.e. `depends_on` that carries no data is ordering rather
  than dependency (scripts/validate-program.mjs, policies/programs-schema.md);
  the return envelope with a SCOPE field, so a failed unit is returned instead
  of the whole batch (scripts/auto-loop/return-envelope.mjs); `split_by` as a
  declared cut dimension on parallel blocks (policies/programs-schema.md); the
  closed lane that no approval opens, distinct from a high threshold
  (hooks/scripts/permission-ladder-guard.mjs, policies/tool-safety.md); and the
  `bad_plan` fix destination for a unit that fails the same correction
  repeatedly (agents/debugger.md, scripts/auto-loop/runner.mjs). The article's
  remaining claims were either already enforced in code (loop with a check that
  can fail, loop-inside-node/graph-between-nodes, worker/code-node/gate) or
  judged disproportionate to mechanize.
